  "confidence": 0.94,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U8", "U4", "M3", "R17"],
      "pins": ["U8.2", "U8.4", "U8.5", "U8.3", "U4.18", "M3.3", "R17.1", "R17.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U8-Pad2)", "Net-(U8-Pad4)", "/V_{EC}", "+3V3", "GND"],
      "observed": "The EC isolated SDA path is not a direct isolated connection. U4 pin 18 (SDA_{1}, isolated EC SDA) is connected only to U8 pin 2. M3 pin 3 (RX/SDA) is connected only to U8 pin 4 and R17 pin 1; R17 pin 2 goes to the isolated /V_{EC} supply. U8 is powered from the non-isolated rails: U8 pin 5 is on +3V3 and U8 pin 3 is on GND. Thus a non-isolated buffer is inserted between the ADM3260 isolated side and the EZO-EC SDA, and its output also drives the isolated /V_{EC} pull-up node.",
      "expected": "Per the specification, U4's secondary isolated I2C pair /SDA_EC/SCL_EC should connect directly to M3 (EZO-EC), with SDA as a bidirectional isolated signal and no non-isolated component crossing the isolation boundary. The isolated EC domain should remain galvanically separate from main +3V3/+5V/+24V/GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"118\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"SDA_{1}\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"119\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad4)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"M3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"RX/SDA\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"R17\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"GND\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R17\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U3 (pH) and U4 (EC) each present a secondary isolated I2C pair (/SDA_pH/SCL_pH, /SDA_EC/SCL_EC) that connects directly to M2 (EZO-pH) and M3 (EZO-EC) respectively"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Each isolated EZO channel (U3 for pH, U4 for EC) derives its own isolated +5V (/V_pH, /V_EC) and isolated ground (/GNDISO_pH, /GNDISO_EC) internally from the ADM3260's isoPower feature, galvanically separate from the main +3V3/+5V/+24V domains."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EZO-EC I2C SDA line is no longer bidirectional between U4 and M3; ACKs from M3 cannot return to the isolator, so EC communication is likely broken. Additionally, the non-isolated buffer output can pull the isolated /V_{EC} domain toward +3V3 or GND through R17, compromising galvanic isolation and potentially loading or damaging the ADM3260/EZO-EC isolated supply.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: the EC isolated I2C SDA path has been interrupted by a non-isolated 74LVC1G34 buffer (U8) powered from +3V3/GND, violating the intended direct isolated connection to the EZO-EC and bridging the isolated EC domain to the non-isolated supply."
}

